{"text": "8/3/18\n\nGEORGETOWN LAw: BEST PRACTICES FOR COURSE DESIGN AND MANAGEMENT\n\nIntroduction\n\nDesigning and teaching a course or seminar for the first time or tenth\ntime is a project that demands significant attention and advance\n\nMemo Contents\n\nplanning. To guide you in that project, we have collected here our basic | Course Syllabi ......---- 2\n\nguidance on drafting course syllabi and related teaching issues. We Course Materials\nhope both new and experienced teachers will find this guidance helpful.\nSome of the information reflects best practices developed by our\n\nCourse Websites ..............++ 8\n\nfaculty. Other guidance is prompted by the requirements of the ABA Evaluating Students ............-. 9\nand federal law. Every institution has its own culture and methods of\noperation. This memorandum will serve as an introduction to both at Evaluating Yourself ............. 13\nGeorgetown University Law Center. Teaching Resources ........0..-. 14\nThe information that follows is designed to take you through several Quick Start Card ....c.ccescseseeee Al\nkey steps in planning to teach. The first section of this memorandum\nSyllabus Template ............... A2\n\ndiscusses drafting a course syllabus. We then review topics such as\nselecting course materials, creating a course website, evaluating\nstudents and providing feedback, and information on teaching support\n\nLearning Outcomes Tips......A3\n\nand resources at the Law Center. Finally, we include a one-page Quick Start card to guide\nyou through your course set-up.\n\nAs you read this memorandum, please keep in mind that there are designated faculty contacts.\nThese Contacts are as follows:\n\nFaculty\n\nContact\n\nTelephone\n\nEmail\n\nPracticum & Simulation\nCourses\n\nKennisha A. Austin\n\n(202) 661-6718\n\nKennisha.Austin@georgetown.edu\n\nFaculty\n\nClinical Courses Patrick Griffith (202) 662-9181 | Patrick.Griffith@georgetown.edu\nJ.D. Adjuncts Sarah Hulsey (202) 662-9041 | Sarah.Hulsey@georgetown.edu\n(nonexperiential)\nLL.M. Adjuncts Tiffany Joly (202) 662-9319 | Tiffany. Joly@georgetown.edu\nFull-Time & U.S.-based | Sally McCarthy (202) 662-9041 | Sally.McCarthy@georgetown.edu\nVisiting Faculty\nInternational Visiting Cara Morris (202) 662-9860 | Cara.Morris@georgetown.edu\n\nExternships\n\nJuliana Siconolfi\n\n(202) 662-4073\n\nJuliana.Siconolfi@georgetown.edu",
